2. Read the code and run it on your own device to learn or do research as an individual.


Ask us first for anything else

Any other use needs Team GG's prior written permission. This includes copying and redistributing it, modifying and using it, running it as a service, and applying it to your work. It applies to commercial and non-commercial use alike, including use by national or local governments and public institutions in their work.

If you would like to use it, please leave a note in this repository's GitHub Issues. Tell us where and how you plan to use it, and we will be glad to look at it with you.


What these terms do not cover

- Code and data from the contest starter kit: the first version of engine/ was moved over from the starter kit's code, and engine/data/ (the ordinance text, ordinance chunks, embeddings, and annex reading results) is as the starter kit made it. Team GG does not claim rights to these parts.
- The data listed in "Data sources and terms" in README.en.md: each keeps its original terms. Tables extracted from OpenStreetMap (place names, roads, parks, and others) are under ODbL 1.0, so anyone may use them under those terms (attribution and share-alike).
- The font (IBM Plex Sans KR, SIL Open Font License 1.1) and outside libraries: each follows its own license.


